<title>GERMANY: SGL Carbon details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>SGL Carbon details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(In millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				1,775  vs 1,556</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		 324    vs 260</p>
<p>    Group return on sales		  18 pct vs 17 pct</p>
<p>    Group return on assets		 25 pct vs 25 pct</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		   288    vs 234</p>
<p>    Group extraordinary costs	    34     vs 0</p>
<p>    Group tax rate			   30     vs 32</p>
<p>    Group net profit			 201    vs 159</p>
<p>    Group net profit under GAAP	  145    vs N/A</p>
<p>    Earnings per share		     9.00 dmk vs 7.61 dmk</p>
<p>    Dividend per share		     2.20 dmk vs 1.67 dmk</p>
<p>    Gross cash flow			  313	vs 260</p>
<p>    Group investments			120	vs 89</p>
<p>    Writedowns				 91	 vs 76</p>
<p>Group equity capital (HBG German</p>
<p>    Commercial Code)			 705	 vs NA</p>
<p>    Group equity capital U.S. GAAP     889	 vs NA</p>
<p>    Equity capital ratio		   43 pct    vs 41 pct</p>
<p>    Workforce				  6,541     5,245</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carbon and graphite group is SGL Carbon AG. SGL reported key 1996 results at the end of January. The results include the acquisitions Polygraph (Poland) and Vicarb (France and U.S.).</p>
<p>The extraordinary cost of 34 million marks results from a five-year management cash incentive plan under which 73 managers obtained three percent of SGL's capital.</p>
<p>Workforce for 1996 includes 1,264 employees at Polygraph and Vicarb. Excluding them, SGL's workforce was unchanged.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
